## Intro
> MD: Keys alone, the last line of the hymn. Vocal comes in on beat 3 of the last bar.
{p} 6m | 1/5:2 57:1 | 1 | 1

## Verse 1
> MD: Keys and vocal. Very simple.
> MD keys: Soft quarter notes in 3/4, left hand on beat 1 of every bar.
> MD bass, drums, gtr: Out.
1 "Amazing grace, how sweet the sound" | 1 | 6m:2 4:1 | 1
1 "That saved a wretch like me" | 1:2 57:1 | 1/3 | 5/2:2 1:1
1 "I once was lost" | 1 | 4 | 1
6m "Was blind, but now I see" | 1/5:2 57:1 | 1 | 1

## Verse 2
> MD: Bass and acoustic guitar come in.
> MD bass: Long notes on 1, follow the inversions (1/3, 5/2, 1/5).
> MD gtr: Soft arpeggio, one note per beat.
@use Verse 1

## Verse 3
> MD: Drums come in. Build a little.
> MD drums: Brushes or rim: kick on 1, rim on 2 and 3.
@use Verse 1

## Verse 4
> MD: Full band, the biggest so far.
> MD drums: Cymbals, fill on the last bar.
@use Verse 1

## Verse 5
> MD: Band drops out, keys stay. Intimate.
> MD bass, drums, gtr: Out. Back in on verse 6.
@use Verse 1

## Verse 6
> MD: Full band back in, the biggest verse. At the end we repeat the last line.
@use Verse 1

## Tag
> MD: Last line again, slowing down. Let the 1 ring until my cue.
> MD drums: Swell on the last chord, no groove.
{mp} 6m "Than when we'd first begun" | 1/5:2 57:1 {rit} | 1 | <1>~
